#### Project-local xschemrc for LVS-form netlisting.
####
#### Identical to design/xschemrc in every respect except one switch, so the
#### two exports can never drift apart in library paths, netlist type or
#### hierarchy handling:
####
####     set lvs_netlist 1
####
#### With that set, xschem renders each device instance from its symbol's
#### `lvs_format` attribute instead of its `format` attribute. For the
#### gf180mcu PDK symbols those two differ in exactly the way LVS needs
#### (libs.tech/xschem/symbols/nfet_03v3.sym):
####
####     format     = "@spiceprefix@name @pinlist @model L=@L W=@W nf=@nf
####                   ad=@ad as=@as pd=@pd ps=@ps nrd=@nrd nrs=@nrs
####                   sa=@sa sb=@sb sd=@sd m=@m"
####     lvs_format = "@name @pinlist @model L=@L W=@W nf=@nf m=@m"
####
#### i.e. the simulation form is `XM1 ... nfet_03v3 ...` (an ngspice
#### subcircuit call, since the gf180mcu ngspice models are subcircuits),
#### while the LVS form is `M1 ... nfet_03v3 L=... W=... nf=... m=...` -- a
#### plain SPICE element whose leading letter names the device class and
#### whose parameters are only the geometric ones. KLayout's
#### `RBA::NetlistSpiceReader` (which the gf180mcu LVS deck drives) reads the
#### second form and cannot evaluate the first form's parameter expressions
#### (`ad='int((nf+1)/2) * W/nf * 0.18u'`).
####
#### Consequence for schematic authoring: in a cell that will be LVS'd,
#### **name each device instance with the SPICE element letter its class
#### needs** -- `M*` for MOS, `R*` for resistors, `C*` for capacitors --
#### because `lvs_format` starts with a bare `@name` and that letter is what
#### tells the reader which element it is looking at.
####
#### Requires xschem >= 3.4.6 (the repo pins 3.4.7 -- see
#### docs/environment-setup.md). xschem 3.4.4, which is what Debian/Ubuntu
#### package, has no `lvs_format` support at all and silently emits the
#### simulation form instead; layout/drclvs.py checks the exported netlist
#### for that and fails loudly rather than handing LVS a netlist it will
#### mis-read.
####
#### Also note `lvs_netlist` must be set **before** the schematic is loaded --
#### `--command "xschem set lvs_netlist 1; xschem netlist"` is too late and
#### silently produces the simulation form. That is why this is an rcfile and
#### not a command-line switch.

set _lvs_rc_dir [file normalize [file dirname [info script]]]
source [file join [file dirname $_lvs_rc_dir] design xschemrc]
unset _lvs_rc_dir

set lvs_netlist 1
